  Package Version Detail:
=> 2.12.0 is a package version number
First number (2) is known as major, second number (12) is known as minor, and the last number (0) is patch.

=> ^ is a caret used with version number
It updates minor and patch versions. Suppose we are using version 2.12.0 and a new version like 2.12.1 or 2.13.0 is released — it will update. But it will not update to 3.0.0.
Caret ^ updates the package only within the same major version.

=> ~ is a tilda used with version number
It updates only the patch version. Suppose we are using version 2.12.0 and a new version 2.12.1 is released — it will update. But it will not update to 2.13.0.
Tilda ~ updates the package only within the same minor version.

=> If we do not use ^ or ~ (just the number), then it locks the package to that exact version.

=> >version → Must be greater than version
=> >=version → Must be equal to or greater than version
=> <version → Must be less than version
=> <=version → Must be equal to or less than version
=> 1.2.x → Matches 1.2.0, 1.2.1, etc., but not 1.3.0
=> * → Matches any version
 
